Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:37:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 018/155] [ae-patch] Color the context ring near a full window
 and label the prompt cache bar

Reid asked on 2026-09-24 for two things in the composer's usage cues:

- The context ring should change color as the session nears the end of
  its context window, the way Claude Code desktop does. Upstream draws
  ComposerContextRing grayscale on purpose. The new
  web/src/lib/aeContextTone.ts holds the steps: normal below 60%,
  warning from 60%, critical from 80%, decided on the rounded
  percentage the tooltip prints. They are earlier than the plan limit
  bars (limitTone, 70 and 90) because a context fills inside one
  session and the harness compacts before 100%, while a plan limit only
  stops work at 100%; limitTone's comment already described the ring's
  steps as the earlier ones. Only the used arc takes the tone, through
  the theme's text-warning and text-destructive tokens, which exist in
  light and dark mode; the button and the track stay muted. The ring
  has no visible percentage label in v0.15.0 (its tests keep text out
  of the bar), so there is no label to color.
- The thin bar under the popover's Context window row (three greys for
  cached, cache write and new input) read as a second meter. Each part
  now has its own chart color (chart-1 blue, chart-3 green, chart-5
  grey, never the warning or destructive colors the bars above use for
  "nearly full"), the legend keeps its dots, and a caption above the
  bar says what it is: "How those tokens were billed (prompt cache)".
  A /context-style breakdown (system prompt, tools, messages) is not
  possible from this data; the status line carries only these counts.

The popover's Context window bar uses contextTone too, so the ring and
the bar always agree.

Upstream files touched: ComposerContextRing.tsx (the import, one class
on the used arc, two doc comment lines) and ComposerContextRing.test.tsx
(the name and comment of the high-usage test, which still passes: the
button stays muted). Tests: src/lib/aeContextTone.test.tsx (the steps,
and the real ring at 50, 65 and 85 percent) and two cases in
AePlanLimits.test.tsx.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
